 side with the same transverse offset, paint the re-entry footprint there, then rotate according to the legend color for that portal.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e87109e9/24/code.py:548:    - Because every obstacle has the same square shape and size, geometry no longer distinguishes them; the repeated color is the portal-pair signal, while the legend still determines only the post-teleport turn.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e87109e9/24/code.py:563:    out, _hits = _trace_portal_beams(base, turns, bg, teal=TEAL)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e87109e9/37/code.py:3:# Name: 对称障碍物加传送门\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e87109e9/37/code.py:20:#      Same-color opposite blockers are the portal pair.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e87109e9/37/code.py:25:#      The teleport breaks the local continuity of the old path, while the symmetric placement makes\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e87109e9/37/code.py:29:#      evidence for portal pairing while keeping the color logic human-trackable.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e87109e9/37/code.py:32:#      portal pairs redirect differently.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e87109e9/37/code.py:33:#    - Exactly one beam axis gets a second portal hit (north/south or east/west, chosen per sample).\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e87109e9/37/code.py:34:#      That keeps the variant visibly richer than \"teleport once\", but avoids tangled 3-hit loops.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e87109e9/37/code.py:44:#    - The four rectangles are built from one symmetric template around the teal square, so portals\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e87109e9/37/code.py:48:#    - The solver assumes portal exits land on background-only lanes. The generator enforces those\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e87109e9/37/code.py:54:#      teleport effect inferable from 2-3 examples.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e87109e9/37/code.py:65:#    - `main()` assumes a beam footprint never overlaps mixed obstacle colors and that portal traces do\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e87109e9/37/code.py:68:#      solver, so the solver stays focused on the visible portal rule.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e87109e9/37/code.py:133:        assert int(np.sum(mask[r0 : r1 + 1, c0 : c1 + 1])) == area, \"portal components must be solid rectangles\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e87109e9/37/code.py:139:def _collect_portals(base: np.ndarray, bg: int, teal: int) -> dict[int, list[tuple[int, int, int, int]]]:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e87109e9/37/code.py:140:    portals: dict[int, list[tuple[int, int, int, int]]] = {}\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e87109e9/37/code.py:147:        assert (a1 - a0, b1 - b0) == (c1 - c0, d1 - d0), \"paired portals must be congruent\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e87109e9/37/code.py:148:        portals[color] = rects\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e87109e9/37/code.py:149:    assert portals, \"at least one portal pair must exist\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e87109e9/37/code.py:150:    return portals\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e87109e9/37/code.py:180:        assert (hr1 - hr0) <= (hc1 - hc0), \"north/south movement must hit a horizontal portal\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e87109e9/37/code.py:181:        assert (hc1 - hc0) == (oc1 - oc0), \"paired portal spans must match\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e87109e9/37/code.py:186:    assert (hc1 - hc0) <= (hr1 - hr0), \"east/west movement must hit a vertical portal\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e87109e9/37/code.py:187:    assert (hr1 - hr0) == (or1 - or0), \"paired portal spans must match\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e87109e9/37/code.py:194:def _trace_portal_beams(\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e87109e9/37/code.py:201:    portals = _collect_portals(base, bg, teal)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e87109e9/37/code.py:234:            assert oc in turns, \"portal color must be listed in the legend\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e87109e9/37/code.py:235:            rects = portals[oc]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e87109e9/37/code.py:237:            assert len(hit_ids) == 1, \"beam must enter exactly one portal component\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e87109e9/37/code.py:241:            assert in_bounds(er, ec), \"portal exit must stay inside the main grid\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e87109e9/37/code.py:242:            assert _obstacle_color_at(base, er, ec, sz, bg, teal) is None, \"portal exit must be on a non-obstacle lane\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e87109e9/37/code.py:248:            assert len(beam_hits) <= 2, \"generator only creates up to two portal hits per beam\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e87109e9/37/code.py:295:    Shoot four teal beams from the source square, but the symmetric obstacle pairs now act as portals.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e87109e9/37/code.py:306:    - If the next step would overlap a colored obstacle, treat that obstacle as a portal: jump to the other\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e87109e9/37/code.py:313:      portals, while the legend only determines how the beam turns after it emerges from the partner copy.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e87109e9/37/code.py:329:    out, _hits = _trace_portal_beams(base, turns, bg, teal=8)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e87109e9/37/code.py:361:def _portal_rectangles(\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e87109e9/37/code.py:420:    rects = _portal_rectangles(sr, sc, sz, t_ns, t_we, gap_ns, gap_we, h_ext, v_ext)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e87109e9/37/code.py:444:        expected, hits = _trace_portal_beams(base, turns, bg, teal=TEAL)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e87109e9/_logs/launch_meta.json:292:    \"name\": \"传送门加统一方块\",\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e87109e9/_logs/launch_meta.json:462:    \"name\": \"对称障碍物加传送门\",\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/271d71e2/25/code.py:25:#   输入里某容器是 4x6 的 5/7 矩形；其上方紧贴一条长度 6 的蓝线作为 head；\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/271d71e2/25/code.py:46:#   - head 是紧贴容器某一整条边的单层实线。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/271d71e2/25/code.py:74:# - `_pick_head_and_dest()` 假设只有一侧会出现“紧贴容器整边的单色 head 线”；\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/d35bdbdc/13/code.py:33:#   - 若目标总是彼此紧贴，裁剪后几乎固定成 3x5/3x6，小样本下很难看出“从整图裁成局部”的规则。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/271d71e2/11/code.py:7:# - 视觉对象延续原题：6 背景，0 黑框容器，内部由 5 灰 / 7 橙组成，9 既画紧贴容器某一边的头线，\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/271d71e2/17/code.py:20:#    具体小例子：一个 3x4 的 5/7 矩形，右侧紧贴一条蓝色(1) head；在更右方还会有两条候选线：\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/bf45cf4b/17/code.py:3:# Name: 不规则精灵对角紧贴\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/6ffbe589/15/code.py:43:#     - 只有 2 层板和 2 个 cue，场景比原题更干净；内层紧贴外层内侧，保证整体仍是一个清晰的大组件。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8e5c0c38/13/code.py:45:#    - 三个对象保持大间隔，噪声紧贴所属精灵，观察者可以明确判断哪些点是附着在哪个对象上的。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/35ab12c3/29/code.py:9:#      2. 该同色边缘像素旁边紧贴一个“异色边缘控制像素”，其颜色固定编码形状类型：\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/28a6681f/37/code.py:73:#   4. 红色终态紧贴或被蓝色顶住，说明后批次受前批次阻挡。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/8b7bacbf/D19/0/code.py:37:#       紧贴 legend 造成视觉混叠，也防止 traced component 意外碰到 legend。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/faa9f03d/17/code.py:51:#        “marker 正上/下方紧贴异色, 左右或上下更远处才是本色” + “输出中本线会分两轮向外长回来”.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/4a21e3da/30/code.py:32:      其中 TL/TR/BL/BR 去四角; TM/BM 去中心条带(位于 c1,c2 之间且紧贴 r 上下)。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/5545f144/18/code.py:26:#       three cells to the right, the old task would simply teleport the visible triangle.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/80a900e0/15/code.py:19:    - 菱形仍是 5x5 bbox 内的 8 像素空心轮廓；外侧线段仍是紧贴某条边的短对角段\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b9e38dc0/3/code.py:55:#    - 为了避免起点或反射点紧贴 wall 造成 fill 颜色误判, 再额外要求 mover 距 wall >= 3 且路径长度 >= 3.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D12/1/code.py:78:#     ones instead of vanishing or teleporting\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/45a5af55/14/code.py:43:   - 原逻辑默认新外框总是紧贴旧结构：`new_n = cur.shape[0] + 2 * h`。现在这个假设失效，\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/291dc1e1/13/code.py:66:- 输出只使用一个简单对齐规则：水平紧贴、垂直居中，因此可读性比额外加间距或分组更强。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/14/code.py:18:#   缩回为左上角那块 2x2，使放大后的彩色部分仍紧贴红锚。这和原题的“尺寸比=1 所以只镜像不放大”\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/29/code.py:23:      - 每个起点边上紧贴一个箭头色像素, 箭头偏移方向就是初始方向; solver 不再从边界位置硬推方向。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db0c5428/29/code.py:3:# Name: 可变块大小+图案紧贴角落\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/1ae2feb7/29/code.py:23:#   原题：near 从列 5 起涂 5,6,7,8...，far 从列 5 起涂 5,7,9...，且不覆盖；几乎紧贴 separator 就着色。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a6f40cea/39/code.py:59:#    - 新增的“为什么停下”并不靠颜色暗示，而靠几何关系：路径停止的位置总是紧贴另一条已占住的路径，\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a47bf94d/1/code.py:179:    \"\"\"Undirected adjacency on visible wire pixels only (5/8, excluding 9 teleport behavior).\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/7c66cb00/D5/1/code.py:5:# Change: 条从底部向上堆叠，条间恰好间隔1行背景色，最底部条紧贴网格底边...\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/28/code.py:11:    终态车道记作 [p0, p1, p2, p3, ...]，其中 p0 紧贴目标墙，p1 在其后一格，依此类推。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/28/code.py:41:    输出则变成紧贴远端墙的连续密集堆叠。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/13/code.py:3:# Name: 紧贴墙壁像素+反射路径\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a32d8b75/10/code.py:34:#    - marker panel 仍然紧贴 frame 下方，而不是漂浮到任意高度，避免布局杂乱。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/8f3a5a89/D14/1/code.py:37:#   - 保持原题的装饰墙机制，但把可见装饰墙限制在边框深处，避免装饰墙紧贴边界导致“为什么\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/2b83f449/3/code.py:13:#      Tokens no longer \"teleport to the unique exit\". They keep moving in their\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/e12f9a14/D6/1/code.py:40:#     - 这样输出主要由若干条干净的直线段组成，终点通常紧贴某个框架边缘，规则更整洁。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/2b83f449/11/code.py:26:       original: token effectively teleports to c=4, then falls\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/2b83f449/7/code.py:24:#    a token at an edge effectively teleports to that exit and drops. Here that hidden motion is\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/2b83f449/9/code.py:20:#   is at col 6. In the base task it would simply teleport to that unique exit.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/80a900e0/D2/1/code.py:11:#    因此生成器做一个必要的适配：每条外线段仍保持原来的方向、仍紧贴对应菱形边外侧，\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/2b83f449/6/code.py:20:#   This combo instead uses the vertical entry portal at column 4 and fills (8,4), then\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/2b83f449/6/code.py:34:#   lower entry portal, because that portal contributes only three passable cells. The\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/2b83f449/6/code.py:36:#   rejects samples unless every portal bucket fits without collision.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/2b83f449/6/code.py:45:#   compact vertical token piles at final entry portals; this is much easier to distinguish by\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/2b83f449/6/code.py:50:#   2. at least one terminal portal receives >=2 tokens, producing a genuine vertical stack,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/2b83f449/6/code.py:194:    portal_buckets: dict[tuple[int, int], list[dict[str, int]]] = defaultdict(list)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/2b83f449/6/code.py:199:            portal_buckets[(int(rec[\"row\"]), entry)].append(rec)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/2b83f449/6/code.py:204:    for (r, entry), bucket in sorted(portal_buckets.items()):\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/2b83f449/6/code.py:498:        raise RuntimeError(\"invalid upward portal packing for this grid\")\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/6e453dd6/32/code.py:3:# Name: 精灵已紧贴分隔线+全发射\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/80a900e0/D13/0/code.py:20:    - 外侧短对角线段仍紧贴菱形四边之一，射线仍只从线段两个端点出发\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/cbebaa4b/D2/2/code.py:18:      - 主体色只能来自 {1, 8}，在输出中形成紧贴锚点的“内环”。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e12f9a14/14/code.py:39:#     - 障碍物本身保持原样不被覆盖，终点总紧贴在它们或框墙之前一格，因此人眼能直接看出“没穿过去”。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8698868d/37/code.py:41:#    - frame 仍是紧贴的规则网格，sprite 仍放在网格外的背景区，使用 `random_free_location` 保证不重叠、不越界。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e12f9a14/9/code.py:40:#     - 单缺口、单直线、路径互斥，使输出主要是几条干净的细线段，终点紧贴别框边缘或网格边界。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/20270e3b/18/code.py:24:- 具体小例子：若 base connector 在第 4 列、长度 3，body 紧贴第 3 列；plug 的\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/20270e3b/18/code.py:25:  connector 也长度 3，body 紧贴 connector 右侧。对接时 plug connector 被平移到\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/142ca369/9/code.py:75:      - 提示条紧贴箭头，颜色来源是局部且可配对的。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/e87109e9/D17/2/code.py:3:# Change: 所有障碍物功能相同——都触发转弯，只是转弯方向不同（由图例决定）... → 传送门障碍物\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/e87109e9/D17/2/code.py:12:# Design analysis for the D17 portal variant\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/e87109e9/D17/2/code.py:20:#    - A teal sz x sz beam that would step into a portal bar does not paint that bar. It jumps to\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/e87109e9/D17/2/code.py:29:#    - Two portal colors are used per instance, each repeated twice. This gives repeated evidence for\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/e87109e9/D17/2/code.py:31:#    - The legend still matters, because teleport alone is not enough: exit direction depends on the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/e87109e9/D17/2/code.py:33:#    - At least one beam in every sample performs a second portal interaction, so the variant is not\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/e87109e9/D17/2/code.py:34:#      visually reducible to \"straight teleport once and stop\".\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/e87109e9/D17/2/code.py:40:#      portal rule that would silently implement the original task. The new logic must change position\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/e87109e9/D17/2/code.py:41:#      first (teleport) and only then rotate.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/e87109e9/D17/2/code.py:42:#    - Old generator assigned each side its own color. That prevents portal pairing entirely. The new\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/e87109e9/D17/2/code.py:49:#    - The teal square is placed strictly inside the portal lanes so every beam reaches its first portal\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/e87109e9/D17/2/code.py:50:#      through background cells before any teleport occurs.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/e87109e9/D17/2/code.py:58:#    - The beam paints only background cells, never overwriting portals, so obstacles remain legible.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/e87109e9/D17/2/code.py:61:#    - Only two portal colors are active per sample, keeping the color logic small and observable.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/e87109e9/D17/2/code.py:67:#    - `main()` assumes portal paths do not cycle. The generator chooses required/excluded spans and\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/e87109e9/D17/2/code.py:137:        assert int(np.sum(mask[r0 : r1 + 1, c0 : c1 + 1])) == area, \"portal components must be solid rectangles\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/e87109e9/D17/2/code.py:143:def _collect_portals(base: np.ndarray, bg: int, teal: int) -> dict[int, list[tuple[int, int, int, int]]]:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/e87109e9/D17/2/code.py:144:    portals: dict[int, list[tuple[int, int, int, int]]] = {}\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/e87109e9/D17/2/code.py:151:        assert (a1 - a0, b1 - b0) == (c1 - c0, d1 - d0), \"paired portals must be congruent\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/e87109e9/D17/2/code.py:152:        portals[color] = rects\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/e87109e9/D17/2/code.py:153:    assert len(portals) >= 1, \"at least one portal pair must exist\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/e87109e9/D17/2/code.py:154:    return portals\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/e87109e9/D17/2/code.py:184:        assert (hr1 - hr0) <= (hc1 - hc0), \"north/south movement must hit a horizontal portal\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/e87109e9/D17/2/code.py:185:        assert (hc1 - hc0) == (oc1 - oc0), \"paired portal spans must match\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/e87109e9/D17/2/code.py:190:    assert (hc1 - hc0) <= (hr1 - hr0), \"east/west movement must hit a vertical portal\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/e87109e9/D17/2/code.py:191:    assert (hr1 - hr0) == (or1 - or0), \"paired portal spans must match\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/e87109e9/D17/2/code.py:198:def _trace_portal_beams(\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/e87109e9/D17/2/code.py:205:    portals = _collect_portals(base, bg, teal)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/e87109e9/D17/2/code.py:238:            assert oc in turns, \"portal color must be listed in the legend\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/e87109e9/D17/2/code.py:239:            rects = portals[oc]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/e87109e9/D17/2/code.py:241:            assert len(hit_ids) == 1, \"beam must enter exactly one portal component\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/e87109e9/D17/2/code.py:245:            assert in_bounds(er, ec), \"portal exit must stay inside the main grid\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/e87109e9/D17/2/code.py:246:            assert _obstacle_color_at(base, er, ec, sz, bg, teal) is None, \"portal exit must be on a non-obstacle lane\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/e87109e9/D17/2/code.py:252:            assert len(beam_hits) <= 2, \"generator only creates up to two portal hits per beam\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/e87109e9/D17/2/code.py:260:    Launch four teal beams from the central square, but colored blockers now work as paired portals.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/e87109e9/D17/2/code.py:265:      appears exactly twice, forming a same-color portal pair.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/e87109e